{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>YHWH Elohei ha-shamayim.</b> Rashi's comment: and not 'Elohei ha-aretz,' because the people of the world did not recognize Him. But by this line of reasoning you would have to explain that, as it were, before He created anything in the world, He was not 'Elohei ha-shamayim.' And on this model the prophet said: 'Before Me no El was formed, and after Me there shall be none' — after knowledge of His divinity ceases from the mouths of creatures, that is, after the entire world has passed and been nullified, there will be no fear [of Him] at all; only He alone, without beginning and without end. And for this reason there is no mention of kingship in the first blessing of the prayer of the Shemoneh Esreh, for it is not applicable to say 'King of the universe, Elohei Avraham' — since at the time He first became 'Elohei Avraham,' He was not yet king over all the world." "<b>Who took me from my father's house.</b> That He distanced me from my kin to give me this land, and He does not want my seed to be distanced from here. Therefore I know that He will send His angel, etc., to fulfill His promise to give this land to his seed — for if His intent were not so, why did He bring me here?" "<b>And you shall take a wife for my son.</b> This is prophecy and not prayer, and that is what is written further on: 'as YHWH spoke.' And some interpret <b>He will send His angel</b> as a prayer, for if it were prophecy, what is the meaning of what is written: 'and if the woman does not consent to go'? Behold, it was prophesied that his way would succeed — [so why mention the possibility of refusal?]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The text reads תפלת של שמונה עשרה; the redundant של may be a copyist dittography. Translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:39.071511028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}